{"name":"Soufflé","hex":"#edd1a8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soufflé","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A baked dish made from beaten egg whites and various other ingredients, usually prepared and served in a small earthenware bowl (ramekin)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Decorated with very small drops or sprinkles of colour, as if blown from a bellows."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/souffl%C3%A9"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soufflé","blocks":[{"text":"A soufflé is a baked egg dish originating in France in the early 18th century. Combined with various other ingredients, it can be served as a savoury main dish or sweetened as a dessert. The word soufflé is the past participle of the French verb souffler, which means to blow, breathe, inflate or puff."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Bacon_and_Cheddar_Cheese_Souffl%C3%A9.jpg/330px-Bacon_and_Cheddar_Cheese_Souffl%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Souffl%C3%A9","wikidata":"Q846376"},{"title":"Soufflé (programming language)","blocks":[{"text":"Soufflé is an open source parallel logic programming language, influenced by Datalog. Soufflé includes both an interpreter and a compiler that targets parallel C++. Soufflé has been used to build static analyzers, disassemblers, and tools for binary reverse engineering. Soufflé is considered by academic researchers to be high-performance and \"state of the art,\" and is often used in benchmarks in academic papers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Souffl%C3%A9_(programming_language)","wikidata":"Q117086146"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Lemon_Souffl%C3%A9.jpg/250px-Lemon_Souffl%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/Lemon_Souffl%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=